The names of subdirectories in this directory follow a specific format that is
derived from the name of the corresponding RPM package.

The format is <name>-<version>, where <version> is the version number of the
package, as provided by the upstream vendor.

If the package is a Python package, the <name> is the part of the RPM package
name that follows "awips2-python-". Otherwise <name> is the part that follows
"awips2-".

The <name> is case-sensitive.

For example, consider the package awips2-python-numpy version 1.16.2. The name
of the corresponding FOSS directory must be "numpy-1.16.2".

For a non-Python example, look at awips2-hdf5 version 1.12.0. The FOSS
directory is called "hdf5-1.12.0".

Failure to follow the above conventions may result in your package failing to
build.
